WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.767
-Welcome back to the show,
Bashir, it's always good

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.567
to see you, buddy.
-Nice to see you, too, Jimmy.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.367
It's nice to be here.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.000
-I brought this up once before

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.200
when you were on the show,
but you were a writer

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.400
on "Late Night."
-"Late Night with Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.734
-For four years.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:17.267
-Great TV show,
just really solid writing.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.334
-I mean, yeah,
the writing was solid.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:20.901
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah. We had you --

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.400
-The host was great, too.
Loved him.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.901
-We had you perform, as well,
because, you know --

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.968
-Yeah, I did a few characters.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.901
-A few bits.
-A few bits and skits.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.801
-Bits and skits.
-Now you're co-starring with --

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.501
-[ Laughs ]
-You looked at the photo.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.167
Now you're co-starring
with Tom Cruise.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:40.033
But before you co-starred
in "Top Gun" with Tom Cruise,

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.367
you were playing
Weird Al --

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.534
Weird Al Roker.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.534
-There it is.
-Is what we did on our show.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.234
That was Weird Al.

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:49.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.734
Do people come up to you
and do any of the bits like...?

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.300
-Yeah, still, every now and
then, I'll be like at CVS

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.601
about to get some toothpaste.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.934
I'll reach for the tube,

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.934
somebody else reach
at the same time,

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.567
our eyes will meet
and he'll be like,

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.133
"Hubble gotchu."

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:08.767
-Hubble gotchu!
Milky J, man. That was my jam.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.701
-Yeah, man. Still got fans.
They love it.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.133
-Your writing partner,
Diallo --

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.534
-Diallo Riddle.
-Diallo Riddle.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.267
I love him.
Please give him my best.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:18.434
-I will, I will.
-You guys met at Harvard.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.868
-We did. We did.
Yeah, we met at Harvard.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.701
In a writing thing or...?

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.701
-No, we met in
an a cappella group.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.067
It was...

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:28.701
It was a bunch of brothers,
and we all went to Harvard

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.400
and we wanted to have
a good name.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.167
So we put our Harvard
brains together

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.567
and we came up with...

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.901
Brothers.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:35.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.934
-Brothers was the name?
-Brothers. Yeah.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.067
-Wow, you really put
some thought into that.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.100
-Then we sort of was like,
"Man, I think

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.367
we should do better than that."

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.100
We were like, "Nah, that's good,
man. Let it happen."

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.534
-Brothers.
-Let it play. Yeah.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:47.033
-What would Brothers do?
-So we would do, like, Shai.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.901
You know, we'd go out to like,
you know, the T stops

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.634
in Boston singing for, like,

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.834
a random dude playing
the pan flute

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:54.801
and the lost MIT student.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:56.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.234
-You would do Shai?
-Oh, we would sing Shai, man.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.200
-"If I ever fall"...
-Oh, you know it?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.534
-I know, I know it, yeah.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:02.968
-You guys want to hear
a little taste of that, maybe?

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.701
-Wait, here. You want a...?

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.534
-Oh! Oh, good. A microphone.

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.501
-We always have one.
Wait, wait.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.634
What's the note gonna be like?

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:14.133
-♪ Mmmmm, mm-mm, mm-mm-mm-mmmm ♪

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.133
-Two, three!

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:24.133
-♪ The very first time
that I saw your brown eyes ♪

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:27.801
♪ Your lips said hello,
and I said hi ♪

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:34.934
♪ I knew right then
you were the one ♪

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.667
♪ But I was caught up ♪
-♪ Caught up ♪

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:40.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:42.234
-♪ I was caught up ♪

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.300
♪ Caught up ♪

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.300
-♪ I was ♪

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.734
-♪ Caught up ♪

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.534
-Alright.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:53.868
That's a new -- that's
a follow-up song.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.434
"I Was Caught Up."
-"I Was Caught Up," yeah.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.667
-Let's talk about
"Top Gun: Maverick."

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.434
-Crazy. Crazy.
-You got the call

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.701
that you're going to be
in "Top Gun."

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:04.000
-Yeah, I was with my mom
and my sister.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.467
I went to the museum,
Art Institute in Chicago.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.667
Folks might know it
from "Ferris Bueller's Day Off."

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.100
It's the museum where
he was in that scene.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.934
And I got the call.

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:15.334
All of a sudden my mom
is jumping up and down,

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.534
my sister, we're high fiving,
and everybody in the museum

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.267
was like,
"Damn, they love Picasso."

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.868
-"Look at that."
-"Look at these guys," yeah.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.501
-They were like, "Hey!
Cubism, right, bruh? Yeah!"

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:26.501
-He's getting hype over art!

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.467
-Getting hype over
the brushstrokes.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.968
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah, it was unbelievable.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.767
-We had a screening for
our office

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.734
and saw it on IMAX,
which I recommend --

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.701
it's just the sound, the visual.
-Gotta see -- yeah.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:40.067
-And you are in every scene
with Tom Cruise, bud.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.100
You're in the first scene.
Dude, you play Hondo.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.400
-Yeah.
-And let me tell you something,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.334
I wish we videotaped
our reaction

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.734
'cause you came on
and we all just went nuts,

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:51.067
like, "Aah! Bashir!"
We're going crazy.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.400
And we have a couple
of new people here

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.334
and they're like,
"Why are you freaking out?"

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.167
-"You guys are going crazy
for THAT guy?"

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.501
"You know Tom Cruise
is up there, too, right?"

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.267
-Yeah. No.
-"No, we know him, though!"

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.267
-You got more applause
and screams.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.634
And you're funny
and you're just awesome in it.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.434
Did you guys bond,
you and Tom Cruise?

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.667
-Oh, man. That's -- he just
texted me yesterday

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:14.834
just 'cause we had a screening.
I feel like I'm bragging

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.300
and it's not even --
I'm just telling a --

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.767
-No, no, no brag.
-He texted me yesterday.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.000
It's interesting.
And, you know,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.834
we had a screening
in my hometown of Chicago.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.467
And he was like,
"How's your family and friends?

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.701
Did everybody love the movie?
Was it great?"

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.200
And I was like,
"Yeah, they loved it."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.868
We would talk about
that stuff on set.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.534
That's actually how we kind
of built camaraderie.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.133
When the cameras weren't
rolling, we would just talk.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.634
We talked about -- he shot
"The Color of Money"

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:36.234
with Paul Newman in Chicago.
It's one of his favorite cities.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.067
I told him about my show,
"South Side."

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.434
He was like, "I want to see it."

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.267
And, you know,
for those of you who, you know,

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.734
Hollywood people,
when they say stuff,

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.300
usually it's like, "Yeah,
you don't mean that," you know?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.501
You're just throwing words
at the universe, right?

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:48.834
And then two weeks later,
I get an email, he's like,

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.367
"Oh, what's up, man?
I thought you were going to

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:51.868
send me that thing
so I can look at it."

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:54.667
I was like,
"Oh, I better do this."

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.601
And so I sent it to him.
He loved it.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.567
He ended up
calling our writer room,

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.234
telling him all the jokes
he liked,

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.234
all his favorite bits,
his favorite actors.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.400
And I'm like, "Hey, guys, uh,

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.868
Tom Cruise wants
to talk to you."

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.400
They were going crazy.
So, yeah.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.934
-He's just legit, right?
-He's legit, man. Yeah.

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.234
-Yeah.
We love you, Tom Cruise.

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:12.300
-Yeah.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.300
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.567
We're showing a clip
from your movie.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.767
-Let's do it. Let's show a clip
from "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:20.767
-Take a look.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.634
[ Door bangs ]

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:26.567
-Admiral.
Uh, just in time, sir.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:28.300
-I'm early. So are you.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.000
Care to explain?

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.300
-Uh, Mav, Admiral Cain
is asking --

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.634
-Ordering.
-...ordering that we
bring her down.

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:40.167
-[ Speech breaking up ]

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:45.167
[ Speaking gibberish haltingly ]

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.033
-This is where we've had trouble
with comms, sir.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.400
It's the Earth's curvature.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.901
Yeah, it's called Earth bulge.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.133
Did anyone offer you a coffee?

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:53.801
Okay.

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.634
-[ Laughing ] Yeah!

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.400
Bashir Salahuddin!

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:00.701
"Top Gun: Maverick"
is in theaters,

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.467
Dolby Cinema and IMAX now.

